            <ArticleTitle>Granuloma annulare of the penis in a seven-year-old boy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>77-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3109/00365599.2010.521190</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Subcutaneous granuloma annulare of the penis is rare, with only 10 cases in the world literature. This paper describes the youngest case ever reported and reviews its clinical features and management.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
